        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: похороны",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "похороны (pokhoróny) — \"a funeral\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "На похороны пришло много людей. Na pokhoróny prishló mnógo lyudéy. A lot of people came to the funeral."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural only; genitive похорон: на похоронах — at the funeral."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "похороны (pokhoróny) is built on хоронить (khoronít) \"to bury\", an inherited Slavic verb whose older sense was \"to keep, to hide away\"; EtymDB lists no parent."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
