              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "смерть (smert) — \"death\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "После смерти отца он стал хозяином фермы. Pósle smérti ottsá on stal khozyáinom férmy. After his father's death he became the owner of the farm."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine; genitive смерти."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "смерть (smert) is inherited through Old East Slavic sŭmĭrtĭ from Proto-Slavic sŭmĭrtĭ (EtymDB), usually explained as sŭ- and the root of умереть \"to die\", PIE mer-."
            }
          ]
        },
